= Generalization — Simple =

'''Generalization''' means a machine-learning system works on new examples, not only the data it trained on.

A model can memorize or fit its training examples very well and still fail on new data.

That is why machine learning uses held-out validation and test data.

Generalization on new data from the same kind of source is different from working after the world or data distribution changes.

The second problem is called distribution shift or out-of-distribution robustness.

